+# SI-P3 v1 engineering contract
+
+Status: **ENGINEERING_ONLY / NO_LIVE / NOT_RUNTIME_READY**. This additive package does not authorize scientific collection, training, evaluation, preflight, or a launch. It preserves the original R19 and bootstrap protocol, prompts, producer, trainer, configs, fingerprints, evidence and failed operations. Its recovery-target exception is conditional on a separate future SI-P3 authorization. There is no learned selector or additional treatment.
+
+## Boundaries and calls
+
+`contract.freeze_plan` accepts only canonical TRAIN identity/family/seed metadata for exactly 96 unique tasks. Family counts 35/26/16/9/10 and the frozen balanced family-by-cutoff matrix are checked before any environment construction; d is 5/10/15/20, globally 24 each. `reservations.bind_reservations` first authenticates caller-supplied original reservation bytes against frozen SHA2566ce8a32a2345b59ecdef9c28c3a341e9c0801b8105f79895f9b2cb9545a4937e, verifies the exact A96 identity/family set against explicit caller seed metadata, then invokes the same freeze_plan. A quota-preserving D48/E600 substitution fails. Historical expected digest cannot be overridden or replaced by a header claim. The returned typed slots stay in memory; this package writes no real-task schedule/argv or task body. Synthetic fixtures use an explicitly separate digest branch. Engineering48 and evaluation600 remain reserved; 395 nonlight and two light are not run. There is no automatic384 continuation.
+
+`collector.Collector` -> source P0 generation/step -> old full source CONTINUE result -> preassigned prefix -> exact reset and d source Action-ID replays -> frozen Stage1/Stage2 -> one teacher action -> **same environment, immediate P0 suffix**, total horizon50. Source continuation labels and costs reference old source receipts, with no extra baseline generation or replay. Actor parser is the existing P0 bare-ID parser; teacher prompts/parsers are the frozen R19 two_stage_v2 bare-ID functions and the P0 prompt is unchanged. P0 source/suffix selection preserves parse_p2_selection independently of EOS completeness; raw cap/completion flags remain evidence, while Stage1/Stage2 teacher completeness stays strict. EOS at a cap is complete. Empty maps, early source termination and unexecuted invalid teachers retain all planned slots; unexecuted YT is null. Success remains done && reward>0. Technical exceptions stop the entire campaign; incomplete units never become a failed-task zero, and remaining slots are explicitly unattempted.
+
+`ProducerAdapter` strictly adapts the existing raw generation dictionary with explicit adapter-state receipts. It checks rendered input, IDs, output decode, token counts, EOS/completion, greedy/thinking flags, cap and P0-vs-base mode. Identity/operation names are owned once by the collector; producer output cannot overwrite them. `EnvironmentAdapter` uses the existing normalized P0 environment interface. The frozen wrapper leaves Task.family=None, so the new adapter derives it from the verified canonical task ID and rejects conflicting explicit family values. Empty terminal maps are supported; an unreported map (None) remains fail-closed rather than silently becoming a complete map. Actual terminal map availability remains unverified without future authorized execution. All backend/environment construction is supplied through runtime ports. Both ports and the collector default to disabled; only explicitly marked synthetic software ports are admitted. Live mode is always rejected. A future real driver must independently authenticate actual active-adapter state, model/input/module origins and resource ownership; a raw receipt declaration alone does not prove an actual adapter switch. No model/environment driver is shipped.
+
+`evidence.Journal` creates a fresh append-only fsynced hash chain with a unique run ID. Existing output is refused. `UnitRegistry` checks run/task/seed/kind/index/start and referenced action receipts online, then starts each physical identity once; a failed started call retains an unknown/open reservation and cannot be retried in that run. These are per-run software contracts, not an issued cross-run scientific execution clearance. Before any generation, exact rendered input IDs and the full output cap are reserved. Reset/replay/actions count physically, once. Final output releases unused reserved tokens only after a matching completed receipt. Global caps8496/9792/138240, input16M/per-call8192 and allocated GPUs multiplied by monotonic ownership duration4device-hours may only tighten. Zero allocated devices in CPU software evidence is not a GPU feasibility measurement. A future resource owner must start the allocation clock at acquisition and bind the actual device count; inference latency is never substituted.
+
+`audit.audit_run` rechecks the raw receipt chain, causal public input, real parser result, every Action-ID/map/command/transition, exact replay, in-place handoff, terminal predicate, old suffix references and full physical costs. It detects semantic tampering even after all hashes and references are recomputed. `logical_costs` derives separate CONTINUE/K1 and invalid teacher-attempt costs from authenticated references; it causes no new debit. This is an engineering integrity consumer, not a confirmatory statistical reporter.
+
+## Pool, background and adoption
+
+`data.build_pool` audits the complete run, applies the same mechanical Q and2048 whole-sequence fit to every row, and deduplicates exact public-input/command before B/C membership. All96 dispositions, ineligible/invalid cases, harms and both failures stay in the denominator. B_pool is Q and YT1; C is its Y0=0 subset. There is no neutral-only B.
+
+S120 uses the fixed dataset SHA and the **complete original895-task five-family expert_train identity hash**, not a caller-selected subset. Tasks are ranked by SHA256 UTF8(`SI-P3-S-v1\n` + family + `\n` + canonical_task + `\n`), with quotas44/32/20/11/13. Within each selected task, eligible existing train rows are ranked by SHA256 UTF8(`SI-P3-S-row-v1\n` + task + `\n` + str(step_index) + `\n` + prompt_sha256 + `\n` + completion + `\n`), then step index. Selected tasks without a qualified full-map, public, format-correct2048-fit row cause NOT_READY; no task replacement is permitted. The historical loader reads an explicitly supplied already-consumed expert dataset; no new task body is opened. Synthetic tests bind a separate explicit synthetic file hash and cannot attest to actual S readiness.
+
+`adopt_once` waits for all96 and checks Q>=72 (family22/17/10/6/7), C and neutral each>=24 (family9/6/4/2/3). C and B hashes each use domain + newline + family + newline + canonical task + newline. Fixed C24 is chosen once. B24 is drawn once from the entire B_pool within family-by-actual-shifted-ID-plus-EOS-length cells matching selected C. At least8 selected B must be neutral, both selected sets need>=20 public projections, and B/C multisets differ. Failure stops that fixed draw; no B exclusion, C redrawing or token-based repair is attempted.
+
+## Continuation and actual masks
+
+`paired_slots` joins the same S120 rows to each24 new examples. Each paired new slot has equal actual shifted target length. One seeded42 permutation per epoch is shared between arms, as are microbatch2 boundaries and accumulation8. `CompletionCollator` right-pads by position; prompt/padding labels are -100 while genuine EOS remains supervised even when EOS=PAD. `audit_exposure` checks actual CausalLM-shifted labels at every microbatch and update, exactly two exposures/task,18 updates, and cumulative new-example and whole-arm nonpadding prompt ratios each<=1.05. Whole maps and targets are never truncated. Character counts are not used as token counts.
+
+`continuation.load_p0_continuation` calls **PeftModel.from_pretrained(base, existing_adapter, is_trainable=True)**. It does not construct a base or a new LoRA. The current entry is gated to a <=1M-parameter CPU software toy and rejects live/Qwen3. `Final18Controller` constructs a fresh optimizer, updates LoRA only, consumes exactly the paired schedule, divides summed loss by each update's actual target-token denominator, and saves only final update18 without validation selection. Output overwrite/resume, extra epochs/steps, fresh-adapter substitution, independent shuffle and drop-last are rejected. CPU tests use an explicitly documented fp32/non-fused exception and a tiny saved adapter, not actual8B/P0 weights. The original recipe (r32/alpha64/dropout.05/all-linear, seed42,2epochs,144 rows,18 updates, lr1e-4, cosine/warmup.03/clip1) stays fixed in the versioned engineering contract. **No real training driver is provided.**
+
+## Verification and limits
+
+The nonempty five-family synthetic path substitutes only raw generation/environment I/O. All orchestration, public prompts, parsers, journal, registry, integrity, Q, selection, collator and controller are production functions. CPU PEFT tests save an original tiny adapter with nonzero LoRA weights, load equal B/C initializations through the real PEFT API, execute18 software updates each, retain frozen base parameters, save final-only and reload exact weights. Cached real-tokenizer checks use only synthetic public strings and never load a neural model. Software tests cannot establish real data yield, cross-run authorization, actual P0 warm-start, GPU completion feasibility, semantic learning value or final efficacy. The JSON schemas describe wire shapes; runtime validators enforce the stronger semantic links. No additional schema dependency is installed.
+
+Before any real use, Sol must independently review the exact frozen engineering SHA, actual tokenizer/collator and complete resource/runtime bindings, task/use isolation, actual P0 continuation setup and output protection. Then a fresh explicit human scientific release is still required. A new pool that passes engineering guards only establishes that a small training dose can be constructed; it does not authorize training or evaluation and does not prove improvement. Future confirmatory statistics remain a separate specification in the SI-P3 authority protocol, with CONTINUE history unchanged. Historical5142 generations/7949 reset-inclusive environment operations are untouched; current real scientific increment remains0.
